    {
      "id": "s1",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "PAPER",
      "headline": "Apple's humanoid learned in simulation",
      "source": "arXiv:2611.06908 · Apple",
      "sourceDate": "Nov 4, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06908",
        "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.06908v1",
        "https://apple-aiml-research.github.io/ml-halo/",
        "https://github.com/apple-aiml-research/ml-halo"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story one. Apple researchers have published a paper on a humanoid robot system called HALO.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/halo_clip_intro.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The robot sits on chairs, and steps sideways through half-open doors.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/halo_clip_sitdoor.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It crouches and crawls under tables, and pushes boxes.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/halo_clip_crawlpush.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Some robots learn from examples that people record by steering them by hand. HALO skipped that step.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "🕹️",
              "title": "Recorded by people",
              "sub": "Humans steer the robot to make examples",
              "cue": "steering"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "🏠",
              "title": "HALO",
              "sub": "Practice in simulated homes",
              "cue": "skipped"
            }
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Instead, it practiced in a thousand computer-generated homes.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/halo_abs_homes.png",
            "stamp": "Preprint"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Think of a flight simulator, but for a robot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "✈️ A flight simulator for robots"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The computer builds a house, plans the robot's movements, and renders what its camera would see.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "🏠",
                "label": "Build a home",
                "sub": "generated by computer",
                "cue": "builds"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🧍",
                "label": "Plan the motion",
                "sub": "whole-body moves",
                "cue": "plans"
              },
              {
                "icon": "📷",
                "label": "Render the view",
                "sub": "what the camera sees",
                "cue": "renders"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Here's that training pipeline on Apple's project page.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/halo_train_c.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Apple, HALO project page"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The real robot is a Unitree G1, with a camera on its head and a Mac mini in a backpack.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/halo_robot_c.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Apple, HALO project page"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "An off-the-shelf vision-language model, an A I that reads both images and text, does the planning.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "acronym",
            "letters": [
              {
                "letter": "V",
                "word": "Vision"
              },
              {
                "letter": "L",
                "word": "Language"
              },
              {
                "letter": "M",
                "word": "Model"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It breaks a plain-language request into steps, like crouch under the table, then push the box.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/halo_clip_steps.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Then the test. Six real homes it had never seen, which were never scanned or mapped.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/halo_clip_realhome.mp4"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Across three hundred sixty real trials, it succeeded ninety-one percent of the time.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/halo_abs.png",
            "stamp": "Preprint"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters: training data made by computers scales with computing power, not with human hours.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "⏱️",
              "title": "Human-recorded data",
              "sub": "Limited by people's time",
              "cue": "human"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "🖥️",
              "title": "Simulated data",
              "sub": "Scales with compute",
              "cue": "computing"
            }
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "And Apple has released the code for making the data, training, and running it on the robot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/halo_demo_42s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Apple, HALO project page"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. That ninety-one percent is for single tasks, like walking to an object or sitting down.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/halo_single.png"
          },
          "section": "reality"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Longer chains of tasks were tested in just one real home. And this is a preprint, with the team's own tests.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Trained only in simulated homes",
                "cue": "Longer"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Multi-step tasks: 1 real home",
                "cue": "one"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Preprint, the team's own tests",
                "cue": "preprint"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "PAPER",
      "headline": "A real-world test arena for robot brains",
      "source": "arXiv:2611.02497 · robocolosseum.ai",
      "sourceDate": "Nov 2, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.02497",
        "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.02497v1",
        "https://robocolosseum.ai/"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story two opens with a line from its own trailer. Every robot looks good in a demo.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/rc_trailer_2s.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Video still: RoboColosseum trailer, robocolosseum.ai"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "RoboColosseum is a network of real robots that tests robot software with the same rules everywhere.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/rc_clip_network.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It works like a blind taste test.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "🥤 A blind taste test"
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Two unnamed models try the same new instruction in the same scene. The evaluator picks the better run, or calls a tie.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "💬",
                "label": "One instruction",
                "sub": "new, same scene",
                "cue": "instruction"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🤖",
                "label": "Two unnamed models",
                "sub": "each try it",
                "cue": "unnamed"
              },
              {
                "icon": "⚖️",
                "label": "Evaluator picks",
                "sub": "better run, or a tie",
                "cue": "picks"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The contestants included five vision-language-action models. Robot brains that see, read an instruction, and act.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "acronym",
            "letters": [
              {
                "letter": "V",
                "word": "Vision"
              },
              {
                "letter": "L",
                "word": "Language"
              },
              {
                "letter": "A",
                "word": "Action"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Plus three frontier A I agents, tested across four kinds of robot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/rc_embod.png",
            "stamp": "Preprint"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "From a small SO-101 arm, to two-armed stations, to a Unitree G1 humanoid.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/rc_clip_fleet.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Across five thousand six hundred ninety-nine head-to-head comparisons at one hundred twenty-four sites,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/rc_clip_sites.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "the general A I agents rivaled the specialized robot models.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/rc_abs.png",
            "stamp": "Preprint"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "But every system struggled to finish open-world tasks reliably.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/rc_trailer_18s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: RoboColosseum trailer, robocolosseum.ai"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The starkest result. On the G1 humanoid, no model completed any of the five tasks.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "0 of 5 humanoid tasks completed",
            "sub": "Average progress: 13.3% to 23.2%"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Average progress ranged from thirteen point three to twenty-three point two percent.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/rc_g1.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Rankings also shifted from one kind of robot to another.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/rc_kendall.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters: every run, failures included, is published on Hugging Face.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/rc_failures.png"
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "So others can study the runs, or train on the data.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/rc_clip_runs.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. This is a preprint, and the organizers, including Hugging Face, ran the evaluation themselves. The results are rankings, not success rates.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Real robots, 124 sites, runs published",
                "cue": "preprint"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Organizers ran the evaluation",
                "cue": "organizers"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Rankings, not success rates",
                "cue": "rankings"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "reality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "Zipline raises $1.5B for drone delivery",
      "source": "zipline.com newsroom",
      "sourceDate": "Nov 5, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://www.zipline.com/newsroom/zipline-raises-1-5-billion-to-build-nationwide-drone-delivery-network",
        "https://x.com/Keller/status/2118379917503000778"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story three. Drone delivery company Zipline has raised one and a half billion dollars.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/zip_photo.png",
            "credit": "Image: Zipline newsroom"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "That's at a valuation of twenty-one and a half billion dollars, according to Zipline's announcement.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/zip_raise.png",
            "stamp": "Company announcement"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Zipline's argument: ground delivery is held back by traffic and rising costs, and roads can't keep up.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "🚗",
              "title": "Ground delivery",
              "sub": "Traffic, aging roads, rising costs",
              "cue": "ground"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "🛸",
              "title": "Drone delivery",
              "sub": "Autonomous aircraft fly over it",
              "cue": "roads"
            }
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "It says the money will expand its U.S. manufacturing and hiring, to build a nationwide network.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "🏭",
                "label": "Manufacturing",
                "sub": "expand in the U.S.",
                "cue": "manufacturing"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🧑‍🔧",
                "label": "Hiring",
                "sub": "ramp up",
                "cue": "hiring"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🗺️",
                "label": "Nationwide network",
                "sub": "drone delivery",
                "cue": "nationwide"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The biggest piece. Walmart and Zipline are working together to launch three hundred more sites,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/zip_walmart.png"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "under a new national, multi-year agreement.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Walmart × Zipline",
            "sub": "300 more sites · multi-year agreement"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Zipline says that in October, its median order arrived nineteen minutes after checkout,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/zip_19.png",
            "stamp": "Self-reported"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "compared with thirty-plus minutes for traditional delivery.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 19,
                "suffix": " min",
                "label": "Zipline median, October",
                "cue": "compared"
              },
              {
                "to": 30,
                "suffix": "+ min",
                "label": "Traditional delivery",
                "cue": "thirty"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "And it reports more than one million deliveries in the Dallas-Fort Worth area alone this year.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/zip_dfw.png",
            "stamp": "Self-reported"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Zipline's Keller Cliffton wrote that when they started the company, flying autonomously in the U.S. was illegal.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/keller_tweet.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Post on X: @Keller, Nov 5, 2026"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters: this is a robot system scaling up, with a national retail partner and a nationwide network as the stated goal.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "hub",
            "center": {
              "icon": "🛸",
              "label": "Zipline"
            },
            "spokes": [
              {
                "icon": "🛒",
                "label": "Walmart",
                "sub": "300 more sites",
                "cue": "retail"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🗺️",
                "label": "Nationwide",
                "sub": "the stated goal",
                "cue": "nationwide"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. These numbers come from Zipline itself. And there's no timeline yet for the three hundred Walmart sites.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "$1.5B raise, company announcement",
                "cue": "numbers"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Delivery figures are self-reported",
                "cue": "itself"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "No timeline for the 300 sites",
                "cue": "timeline"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "reality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
